These scripts will take data that has already been loaded into the MySQL
sched tables (see setup/sched_tables.sql) and load them into memcached.

You will need another script to load semester course schedules into
the MySQL tables following the table layout provided.

Settings (DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_USER, DB_PASS, DB_NAME, MEMCACHED_HOST,
MEMCACHED_PORT) are read from modular-sanic's .env file, found by searching
upward from this directory, or named with ENV_FILE=/path/to/.env.  The
scripts need pymysql, pymemcache and environs, which modular-sanic's
requirements already install; VENV names its virtual environment
(default ../venv).

  ./start-encache.sh    load (or reload) the schedules into memcached
  ./start-decache.sh    remove them again

Values are stored as JSON.  After upgrading from a version that stored
Python literals, run ./start-encache.sh once so every key is rewritten
(the API still reads the old format until then).
